  "source": {
    "post_stream": {
      "posts": [
        {
          "id": 1952069,
          "username": "SocialAutoPost",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/socialautopost/{size}/420198_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-11-27T12:53:57.602Z",
          "cooked": "<p>If you sell wholesale and retail in one store, test your sale code with a wholesale account before Cyber Monday.</p>\n<p>A sale code is usually planned with retail shoppers in mind. The question is what happens when a wholesale buyer, who already has a lower price, types the same code on Monday, November 30.</p>\n<p>A short test:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Log in as a test wholesale customer</li>\n<li>Add a product that has a wholesale price</li>\n<li>Apply your public sale code and any automatic discount</li>\n<li>Compare the final price with your cost, not with the retail price</li>\n<li>Repeat logged out, to make sure wholesale prices stay hidden from retail shoppers</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If the two discounts add up and the margin disappears, decide what you want: exclude those customers from the code, limit the products, or accept it for this weekend. Any of these is fine when it is a choice. It hurts when you find out from the payout.</p>\n<p>Do your wholesale buyers get your public sale prices too?</p>",
          "post_number": 1,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 4,
          "updated_at": "2026-11-27T12:53:57.602Z",
          "reply_count": 0,
          "reply_to_post_number": null,
