    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 1913954,
      "summarized_text": "Merchants selling both wholesale and retail through one Shopify store are urged to test public sale promotions with wholesale accounts before a major sale. Because wholesale buyers already receive reduced catalog prices, an additional retail code or promotion can stack on top and unexpectedly erase margins; the same issue can occur when a sitewide automatic discount applies to wholesale orders.\n\nSuggested checks include comparing checkout prices with product costs, confirming wholesale prices remain hidden from logged-out retail shoppers, and reviewing profit after test orders. One contributor notes that native Shopify automatic discounts cannot exclude a wholesale customer segment. Stores using wholesale apps should check discount-combination settings on both wholesale rules and retail promotions, and verify whether retail free-shipping thresholds apply to bulk wholesale carts.\n\nThe discussion offers prevention strategies—exclude wholesale customers, restrict eligible products, or accept the discount knowingly—but reaches no shared decision. The central issue remains a practical risk merchants should test before launching a promotion.",
      "algorithm": "gpt-6-luna",
